      "value": "English translation below.\n\n# Microphone-switching bug—present since the beta version\n\nDescription\n\nWhen I log in via desktop mode and connect a microphone afterward, it doesn’t appear in the list, so I can’t connect it. This worked in the previous version. The issue isn’t resolved unless I restart, so I’d appreciate it if you could fix this as soon as possible.\n\nThis has been happening since the beta version.\n\nReproduction Steps\n\nAfter entering in desktop mode (I haven’t tried VR mode), even if I connect the microphone via USB, it doesn’t appear in the “Change Microphone Audio” section, and it won’t show up until I restart.\n\nIf I connect the microphone via USB from the start and then enter VRCHAT, it appears in the section.\n\nDetails\n\n- Category: Audio\n\n- Frequency: Always\n\n---\n\nplatform: PC (platform: Windows, store: Steam, headset: None)\n\nrawPlatform: WindowsPlayer\n\nclientVersion: 2026.3.3-1919-27c41b24d2-Release\n\nunityVersion: 6000.0.67f1-DWR\n\nIn-Client Report\n\n---\n\n**Log file:** [output_log_2026-10-03_20-02-27.txt](https://api.vrchat.cloud/api/1/file/file_98b2f5d7-db21-42bd-8c8c-91ee898ed966/1/file)\n\nTranslated with DeepL.com (free version)",
